<title>POLAND: Optimus likely to pay 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>Optimus likely to pay 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish software firm Optimus SA  is likely to earmark between 10 and 12 percent of its 1996 net profit for dividend, the president of the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We see about 10 to 12 percent of our profits... earmarked for dividend,&quot; Roman Kluska said.</p>
<p>Optimus earlier said it would earn 17.5 million zlotys this year. Last year Optimus paid 0.6 zlotys of dividend per share.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
